/* THE 106 GLYPH RECTANGLES OF THE PC FONT PAGE, and nothing else: the body of
 * an initialiser list, moved out of game\text.cpp unchanged.
 * Each row is  u, v, width, height, y offset, top shade, bottom shade.
 *
 * It lives in its own file because two programs have to agree on it to the
 * last digit: game\text.cpp fills CharDef[106] with it, and the HD font
 * (specific\hd\hd_font.cpp) matches those same rectangles against the
 * remaster's glyph atlas. The diagnostic tool FontProbe includes this file a
 * third time and would otherwise carry a copy that could drift.
 *
 * u and v are NOT n/256 but n/255 - measured over all 106 rows, the largest
 * distance from u * 255 to a whole number is 0.000133. The classic UV
 * arithmetic in DrawChar treats them as n/256 anyway, which shifts the
 * sampled window by up to one texel towards the right edge of the page; that
 * is Core's own picture and the HD path reproduces it rather than correcting
 * it (see hd_font.cpp).
 *
 * The width and height here are the UNSCALED ones. InitFont overwrites
 * CharDef[i].w/.h/.YOffset in place with the values for the current screen
 * size, so whoever needs the original numbers has to read them here. */

